  "translation": "reception, front desk: Hello, Courtyard Hotel. Mark: Hello! I'd like to book a room, checking in on the nineteenth of September, for five nights. reception, front desk: Certainly: the nineteenth to the twenty-fourth, five nights. For how many people? Mark: Just me. reception, front desk: Would you like a single room, a twin room, or a double? Mark: What's the difference between a twin and a double? reception, front desk: A twin has two single beds, and a double has one big bed. The double is four hundred and eighty a night. It looks straight out onto the courtyard, and it's very quiet. Mark: Then I'll have the double. Does the rate include breakfast? reception, front desk: It does. Breakfast is Beijing street food: soya milk, fried dough sticks, steamed buns. It's from seven to ten in the ground-floor dining room. Mark: Great! What time can I check in? My flight doesn't get in till nine in the evening. reception, front desk: Any time after two. There's someone on reception twenty-four hours a day. Please bring your passport when you check in. There's also a five-hundred-yuan deposit, which we give back when you check out. Mark: Fine. My name's Mark Smith. What time is check-out? reception, front desk: Before twelve noon. Mr Smith, you're all booked. We'll send you a confirmation text in a moment.",
