  "translation": "Dear Mr and Mrs Lin, Hello! I'm safely back in London. I've been getting over the jet lag these last few days, and today's the first chance I've had to write to you. First of all, thank you so much for your warm hospitality! In my nine days in Chengdu you took me for hotpot, to see the pandas and round Kuanzhai Alley, and you invited me into your home for Mid-Autumn. I loved every dish Mrs Lin made, especially the twice-cooked pork. Mr Lin taught me to drink tea from a lidded bowl, and even wore the same shirt as me! I'll always remember all of it. Before, I'd only read in books what a Chinese home is like. At your home, you made me feel I wasn't a guest, but one of the family. That Mid-Autumn evening, when we ate mooncakes and looked at the moon together, was the most memorable night of my trip. After I left Chengdu I spent five days in Beijing. Chen Ming was right: Beijing roast duck is delicious! But the food I miss most is still Mrs Lin's cooking. Xiaoyu's back in London the day after tomorrow. You're welcome to come and visit London one day, and when you do, I'll treat you to Chen Ming's dumplings! The photos are attached. Have a look. Thank you again! Wishing you good health and all the best! Mark 26 September",
