  "translation": "Xiǎo Yǔ: Hi, Mark, are you up? Mark: Just. I slept till ten today. It was wonderful! Xiǎo Yǔ: Me too. The show's over, and today I don't feel like doing anything. Mark: So what shall we do? Xiǎo Yǔ: Nothing! Just wander round, have a look at things, find somewhere for a coffee and a chat. Mark: Good idea! Where shall we go? Xiǎo Yǔ: There's a Christmas market on the South Bank. Let's go and have a look. I hear the mulled wine there's good. You could give it a try. Mark: Sure. When we've had a look round, we can go for a walk along the river. Oh, by the way, now you've graduated, what are your plans? Xiǎo Yǔ: Find a job first, I suppose. London, Shanghai, Melbourne, I'm looking at all of them... hey, we're not talking about that today! Mark: OK, no work talk. Let's talk about Spring Festival, then. Chen Ming says he's going home to Beijing for New Year, and he's asked if I want to come! Xiǎo Yǔ: Really? Spring Festival in Beijing will be so lively! Mark: Of course I want to go! But I'd better look at flights first... Xiǎo Yǔ: No looking at flights today! Today we just wander and chat, and don't think about anything else. See you on the South Bank in an hour!",
