  "translation": "Saturday 29 January. Sunny, minus eight. Today I finally climbed the Great Wall! When I came to Beijing last September I didn't have time, and I've been sorry ever since. This time Chen Ming and his dad took me to Mutianyu. Mutianyu isn't as crowded as Badaling, and in winter there are even fewer visitors. The Wall was even steeper than I'd imagined. At first I didn't think it was hard at all, but the higher we climbed, the steeper the steps and the stronger the wind. After an hour, I was so tired I couldn't feel my legs. Chen Ming kept saying beside me: 'Keep going! You're not a hero till you've climbed the Great Wall!' '不到长城非好汉' is a very famous line from a poem. 非 means 'is not', and a 好汉 is someone brave and remarkable. It means: anyone who hasn't been to the Great Wall isn't a hero. These days, lots of people use it to say: don't be afraid of hard things, and keep going to the end. At the highest watchtower, I looked down: the Wall was like a dragon, running from one mountain all the way to the next. At that moment I felt that however tired I was, it had been worth it. On the way down I took the cable car with Chen Ming's dad, which was quick and comfortable. Now I'm a hero too! Though tomorrow I might not be able to walk...",
