  "translation": "Dà Wèi: Mark, has Fuhe replied? Go on, check your email! Mark: They have, but I daren't look... Emma, you look for me. Ài Mǎ: OK... 'We are very pleased with your proposal, and it has been approved!' And there's one more line: 'Mark, you presented very well in Chinese. I'd give you full marks!' Mark: Really? Our proposal's really been approved! Chen Ming: Brilliant! Tonight's meal is on me! Yóu Měi: Mark, you've come so far. I remember when you first came to the language exchange, all you could say was 'hello' and 'thank you'. Mark: Oh, not really, I've still got a long way to go. Manager Wang talked so fast that day, I only understood most of it. Dà Wèi: Don't be so modest! I've been learning for a year, and I still get nervous as soon as I speak Chinese. What's your secret? Tell me about it. Mark: What worked for me was learning a bit every day, and never missing a day. And chatting with Chinese friends as much as you can. Ài Mǎ: Easy for you to say! You've got Xiaoyu and Chen Ming. Where are we supposed to find teachers like that? Xiǎo Yǔ: You've got us too! Actually, Mark's biggest strength is that he's not afraid of making mistakes. If you get it wrong, you just put it right. Chen Ming: That's right! The first time he came to my restaurant, he said 'sleep' instead of 'dumplings'! Mark: Don't remind me! ...Right, to celebrate, tonight's on me! Xiǎo Yǔ: In my cousin's restaurant? Forget it. He's always like this!",
  "q": {
   "text": "Who says: “好……“我们对你们的方案非常满意，方案通过了！”还有一句：“马克，你的中文讲得很好，我给你打满分！””",
   "options": [
    "Dà Wèi",
    "Mark",
    "Ài Mǎ",
    "Chen Ming"
   ],
   "answer": 2
  }
