  "translation": "Chen Ming: Hello, can you see me? It's already eight in the evening there, isn't it? It's only nine in the morning here. I've just done the vegetable shopping. Xiǎo Yǔ: Yes, we can! This is my flatmate, Huang Li. She grew up in Melbourne. Huang Li (Lily): Hello! Xiaoyu's always saying your dumplings are the best in the whole of London. Chen Ming: Of course! I'm not bragging, but there are no more authentic dumplings in London than mine. Mark: Chen Ming, we've been discussing all day whether Melbourne or London is better. What do you think? Chen Ming: Need you ask? London, of course! Take food: London has every kind of food there is, for instance... Huang Li (Lily): Melbourne's just the same! People here come from all over the world. Italian, Greek, Vietnamese: whatever you fancy, it's here. Chen Ming: What about Chinese food? London's Chinatown is really lively, and it's got Chen Family Dumplings! Huang Li (Lily): Melbourne's Chinatown has a longer history! It's been here since the 1850s, built by the Chinese who came in the gold rush. Chen Ming: Really? I honestly didn't know that. What about the weather, then? Melbourne must be unbearably hot in summer? Mark: That's true, sometimes it's pretty hot. But it's much nicer than winter in Beijing. Last Spring Festival I was so cold on the Great Wall I couldn't speak! Chen Ming: All right, all right. I reckon it doesn't matter which city is best. What matters is who you're with. Mark: I couldn't agree more! Wherever you lot are, that's the best city. Chen Ming: Ha ha, Mark, your Chinese is getting smoother by the day!",
