  "translation": "Xiǎo Yǔ: Mark, this is for you. Don't open it yet... Oh, never mind, open it! Mark: A mug? And what's painted on it is... London and Melbourne! Xiǎo Yǔ: I designed it myself. On one side is the Tube, on the other a Melbourne tram, and in the middle a flat white. Mark: That's so creative! I'll drink my coffee out of it every morning from now on. Xiǎo Yǔ: As long as you like it. The Tube map you gave me has been on my office wall ever since. Mark: Really? ...Xiaoyu, actually I've got some news for you too. Xiǎo Yǔ: What news? From the look on your face, it's good news? Mark: My boss emailed me the day before yesterday. The company wants to send me to work in Shanghai, for at least a year, maybe longer. Xiǎo Yǔ: Shanghai? The client you've been dealing with? Mark: Yes. They're very happy with our designs, and they want me to go over and work with them. Do you think I should go? Xiǎo Yǔ: Need you ask? It's the best chance you could get! You'd speak Chinese every day, and besides... Mark: Besides what? Xiǎo Yǔ: And besides, Shanghai's much closer to Melbourne than London is. It's only about eleven hours on the plane. Mark: Ha ha, I completely agree with you there! I haven't made up my mind yet, but... a chance like this really doesn't come along often.",
