  "translation": "Landlord (Party A): Qian Meihua. Tenant (Party B): Mark. Following friendly discussion, Party A and Party B have reached the following agreement concerning Party B's rental of Party A's property. 1. The property: Party A lets to Party B one south-facing room on the first floor of No. —, Lane —, Yuyuan Road, Changning District, Shanghai, of about sixteen square metres. The kitchen and bathroom are shared with other tenants. 2. Term: from 1 July 2029 to 30 June 2030, twelve months in all. 3. Rent and payment: the monthly rent is 4,500 yuan. The deposit is one month's rent, that is, 4,500 yuan. Rent is paid every three months, and Party B must pay in full within the five days before each period begins. 4. Bills: during the tenancy, water, electricity and gas are paid by Party B according to actual use. The internet is paid by Party A. 5. Use of the property: Party B shall take good care of the property, furniture and appliances. If damage is caused by improper use, Party B shall be responsible for repair or compensation. Party B may not sublet the property to others, or alter its structure, without Party A's consent. 6. Early termination: if either party needs to end the contract early, they shall give the other party at least one month's notice. Without such notice, they shall pay the other party one month's rent as a penalty. 7. Return of deposit: at the end of the tenancy, once Party B has moved out and Party A has found no damage to the property, Party A shall return the whole deposit to Party B within three days. 8. Other matters: Party B shall follow the rules of the lane. A list of the furniture and appliances in the property is attached. 9. This contract is made in duplicate, one copy for each party, and takes effect from the day both parties sign. Party A (signature): Qian Meihua. Party B (signature): Mark. 9 June 2029.",
